00:09:47.408 --> 00:09:49.250
It sucks that we're going into

00:09:49.250 --> 00:09:51.460
non-garage sale season.

00:09:51.460 --> 00:09:53.150
So it's gonna lose some momentum.

00:09:53.150 --> 00:09:55.080
'Cause I do love a good
town-wide garage sale.

00:09:55.080 --> 00:09:56.650
That's actually a fun fact real quick.

00:09:56.650 --> 00:09:57.925
Just this should belong in

00:09:57.925 --> 00:09:58.990
Trash Talk,

00:09:58.990 --> 00:09:59.823
but you know I like

00:09:59.823 --> 00:10:00.810
my content.

00:10:00.810 --> 00:10:03.890
You have to look for
town-wide garage sales.

00:10:03.890 --> 00:10:05.640
That's when the whole town does it.

00:10:05.640 --> 00:10:07.390
That's how you get to 30 or 40

00:10:07.390 --> 00:10:08.950
in a four hour period.

00:10:08.950 --> 00:10:12.354
100 in a four, five hour period instead of

00:10:12.354 --> 00:10:14.600
driving 28 minutes and

00:10:14.600 --> 00:10:15.560
17 to the next one.

00:10:15.560 --> 00:10:16.840
Anyway that's a fun fact.

00:10:16.840 --> 00:10:18.519
My greatest score for

00:10:18.519 --> 00:10:20.441
20 bucks, 40 bucks

00:10:20.441 --> 00:10:24.222
I bought like 5,000 playbills.

00:10:24.222 --> 00:10:25.055
And when I went through it

00:10:25.055 --> 00:10:26.960
I found like three
Brooklyn Dodgers booklets

00:10:26.960 --> 00:10:28.820
that went for like a buck 50 a pop.

00:10:28.820 --> 00:10:32.462
The original Pinocchio
1940-something movie

00:10:32.462 --> 00:10:34.890
that went for a hundred.

00:10:34.890 --> 00:10:37.530
Every Betty Davis went for 20 a pop.

00:10:37.530 --> 00:10:39.680
Judy Garland's went for like 40 to 50.

00:10:39.680 --> 00:10:40.700
- [D-Rock] Where do you find that?

00:10:40.700 --> 00:10:42.390
- It was at a state sale on a Friday

00:10:42.390 --> 00:10:43.740
in Chatham, New Jersey.

00:10:43.740 --> 00:10:46.380
I was on my way to a liquor meeting,

00:10:46.380 --> 00:10:47.840
and I saw the sign, I was a little early,

00:10:47.840 --> 00:10:48.673
I was like

00:10:48.673 --> 00:10:49.506
(mimics tire screeching)

00:10:49.506 --> 00:10:50.660
Went in, and I couldn't believe it.

00:10:50.660 --> 00:10:52.366
First I found a Huckleberry Hound

00:10:52.366 --> 00:10:55.040
1960's stuffed animal for a buck,

00:10:55.040 --> 00:10:56.330
I was like, bang, game over.

00:10:56.330 --> 00:10:57.280
I was so pumped.

00:10:57.280 --> 00:10:58.905
That's a quick 40 on the come up.

00:10:58.905 --> 00:11:01.084
But then I went downstairs
and just saw like

00:11:01.084 --> 00:11:03.370
80 boxes, and I was like,

00:11:03.370 --> 00:11:04.203
what is this?

00:11:04.203 --> 00:11:05.036
I knew nothing about playbills,

00:11:05.036 --> 00:11:06.530
this was pre-smartphone.

00:11:06.530 --> 00:11:08.170
I just went in.

00:11:08.170 --> 00:11:11.440
Bought it, took me 20
minutes to load my car.

00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:13.010
Bailed on the fuckin' meeting,

00:11:13.010 --> 00:11:14.800
drove to my parents' house,

00:11:14.800 --> 00:11:16.870
waited for AJ to get out of high school,

00:11:16.870 --> 00:11:19.152
and fuckin' spent like
nine hours looking up shit.

00:11:19.152 --> 00:11:20.367
(laughs)

00:11:20.367 --> 00:11:21.543
Do you collect pins?

00:11:21.543 --> 00:11:23.423
(laughs)

00:11:23.423 --> 00:11:25.070
- [D-Rock] You gotta wear one.

00:11:25.070 --> 00:11:25.903
(laughs)

00:11:25.903 --> 00:11:27.470
- That's amazing, I will!

00:11:27.470 --> 00:11:29.550
I'm gonna bid on one of 'em.

00:11:29.550 --> 00:11:31.660
I'm gonna wear a pin from now on.

00:11:31.660 --> 00:11:33.270
A little fun fact about today,

00:11:33.270 --> 00:11:35.920
D-Rock had to put tape
on all his batteries

00:11:35.920 --> 00:11:37.970
at the airport in Melbourne,

00:11:37.970 --> 00:11:39.802
on the way to Sydney.

00:11:39.802 --> 00:11:41.670
The other crazy thing is

00:11:41.670 --> 00:11:43.610
we didn't have to get our ticket checked.

00:11:43.610 --> 00:11:44.863
I was so weirded out.

00:11:45.812 --> 00:11:46.813
Nothing.

00:11:48.885 --> 00:11:49.937
Love it.

00:11:49.937 --> 00:11:53.574
(midtempo dance music)

00:11:53.574 --> 00:11:56.593
- [Announcer] Gary Vaynerchuk!

00:11:56.593 --> 00:11:59.426
(audience cheers)

00:12:00.441 --> 00:12:02.229
Was there ever a time when

00:12:02.229 --> 00:12:03.511
you thought that you would fail,

00:12:03.511 --> 00:12:04.464
and if so,

00:12:04.464 --> 00:12:06.020
how did you overcome that?

00:12:06.020 --> 00:12:08.250
- Norman, I think I can potentially fail

00:12:08.250 --> 00:12:09.180
at any moment.

00:12:09.180 --> 00:12:10.620
That's the beauty of
being an entrepreneur,

00:12:10.620 --> 00:12:12.620
you're only as good as your last at-bat.

00:12:13.470 --> 00:12:15.240
So, there's always a sense

00:12:15.240 --> 00:12:17.120
in the back of my mind that I could fail.

00:12:17.120 --> 00:12:19.065
It's why I've always really, really

00:12:19.065 --> 00:12:22.090
even though I grew up a
much bigger boxing fan

00:12:22.090 --> 00:12:23.470
and I'm still a bigger boxing fan,

00:12:23.470 --> 00:12:24.960
there's something I love about

00:12:24.960 --> 00:12:26.160
mixed martial arts

00:12:26.160 --> 00:12:27.610
is that everybody takes an L.

00:12:28.820 --> 00:12:30.040
Right?

00:12:30.040 --> 00:12:30.873
It's just like,

00:12:30.873 --> 00:12:33.600
and I think that if you're
in business for yourself,

00:12:33.600 --> 00:12:34.433
I mean,

00:12:34.433 --> 00:12:35.530
how many people here are entrepreneurs

00:12:35.530 --> 00:12:38.455
and have been for over
five years successfully?

00:12:38.455 --> 00:12:41.640
A lot of us know, it's lonely as fuck!

00:12:41.640 --> 00:12:43.500
I woke up at four o'clock in the morning

00:12:43.500 --> 00:12:44.820
this morning because there's some shit

00:12:44.820 --> 00:12:45.990
going in my L.A. office,

00:12:45.990 --> 00:12:48.640
I had to cancel a trip to Hawaii next week

00:12:48.640 --> 00:12:50.400
for a conference that I
really wanted to go to

00:12:50.400 --> 00:12:52.270
'cause I have to go to L.A. and fix shit.

00:12:52.270 --> 00:12:53.280
When you're an entrepreneur,

00:12:53.280 --> 00:12:56.000
you own your shit, you're a firefighter!

00:12:56.000 --> 00:12:57.820
You're the last line of defense.

00:12:57.820 --> 00:12:59.210
I always think I can fail.

00:12:59.210 --> 00:13:00.280
It's the reason I'm great,

00:13:00.280 --> 00:13:01.330
I think it's like a fighter,

00:13:01.330 --> 00:13:02.390
you go in there and you know that

00:13:02.390 --> 00:13:03.223
any moment,

00:13:03.223 --> 00:13:04.300
even if you're a much better fighter

00:13:04.300 --> 00:13:05.490
than the other person,

00:13:05.490 --> 00:13:07.550
one punch could change the outcome.

00:13:07.550 --> 00:13:09.350
And that's what I think
entrepreneurship is.

00:13:09.350 --> 00:13:10.900
I wake up every morning knowing that

00:13:10.900 --> 00:13:12.920
one punch that I didn't see coming

00:13:12.920 --> 00:13:14.350
can change the outcome of everything

00:13:14.350 --> 00:13:15.450
that I've been doing.

00:13:15.450 --> 00:13:17.540
And that puts me on an edge

00:13:17.540 --> 00:13:19.400
that I like.

00:13:19.400 --> 00:13:22.220
I like being awake and focused

00:13:22.220 --> 00:13:24.220
and most importantly,

00:13:24.220 --> 00:13:25.900
I like that level of humility.

00:13:25.900 --> 00:13:28.090
I genuinely, I promise you here

00:13:28.090 --> 00:13:29.350
out of every fuckin' person here,

00:13:29.350 --> 00:13:31.760
even if you sit here and
your friend brought you

00:13:31.760 --> 00:13:32.670
and you didn't like me,

00:13:32.670 --> 00:13:33.850
and you think I'm shit,

00:13:33.850 --> 00:13:35.950
nobody thinks less of themselves,

00:13:35.950 --> 00:13:38.250
nobody thinks less of
me in this room than me.

00:13:39.250 --> 00:13:40.240
I mean that.

00:13:40.240 --> 00:13:42.970
I am just unbelievably not high

00:13:42.970 --> 00:13:44.330
on my own supply.

00:13:44.330 --> 00:13:45.960
I appreciate the admiration,

00:13:45.960 --> 00:13:47.900
I understand what's happening with me,

00:13:47.900 --> 00:13:49.090
but I promise you,

00:13:49.090 --> 00:13:50.960
if you could read my insides

00:13:50.960 --> 00:13:52.400
on a piece of paper,

00:13:52.400 --> 00:13:54.860
I stand up here knowing I'm not shit,

00:13:54.860 --> 00:13:56.690
and tomorrow it can all go away

00:13:56.690 --> 00:13:58.400
unless I continue to execute,

00:13:58.400 --> 00:14:00.600
and I play on that edge every day

00:14:00.600 --> 00:14:03.476
and I appreciate and I'm flattered,

00:14:03.476 --> 00:14:05.536
but I'm not fucking confused.

00:14:05.536 --> 00:14:07.248
(audience cheers, applauds)

00:14:07.248 --> 00:14:08.748
Thank you, Sydney!

00:14:10.630 --> 00:14:12.162
Thank you guys.

00:14:12.162 --> 00:14:15.293
Thank you so much.

00:14:15.293 --> 00:14:16.126
Get up here.

00:14:16.126 --> 00:14:17.173
D-Rock!

00:14:17.173 --> 00:14:20.282
(audience applauds, cheers)

00:14:20.282 --> 00:14:21.420
Thank you guys.

00:14:21.420 --> 00:14:22.470
See ya.

00:14:22.470 --> 00:14:25.640
- [Female] So do you have any tips

00:14:25.640 --> 00:14:27.670
on how to deliver an idea

00:14:27.670 --> 00:14:30.113
in a way that really
resonates with an audience?

00:14:30.960 --> 00:14:32.480
- My framework is,

00:14:32.480 --> 00:14:34.980
do you first believe
in what you're saying?

00:14:34.980 --> 00:14:37.100
I know that may sound funny

00:14:37.100 --> 00:14:38.920
but a lot of people do things

00:14:38.920 --> 00:14:40.270
for many different reasons.

00:14:40.270 --> 00:14:41.870
Do you actually believe in it?

00:14:41.870 --> 00:14:44.730
Do you understand how
you best communicate?

00:14:44.730 --> 00:14:45.563
Right?

00:14:45.563 --> 00:14:46.610
Is it audio, is it written word,

00:14:46.610 --> 00:14:47.910
is it through design, is it,

00:14:47.910 --> 00:14:50.240
publicly speaking, is it through video?

00:14:50.240 --> 00:14:51.710
And then do you disproportionately

00:14:51.710 --> 00:14:54.058
take into account the psychology

00:14:54.058 --> 00:14:56.730
of the audience that's consuming it

00:14:56.730 --> 00:15:00.770
and the distribution platform
that's delivering it.

00:15:00.770 --> 00:15:03.300
I respect the stage

00:15:03.300 --> 00:15:07.050
the same way that I respect
the Instagram algorithm.

00:15:07.050 --> 00:15:08.610
I understand that there's a platform

00:15:08.610 --> 00:15:10.080
that is delivering the message,

00:15:10.080 --> 00:15:12.040
and I need to play within it.

00:15:12.040 --> 00:15:15.791
And so, for me it's just
respecting all these variables.

00:15:15.791 --> 00:15:17.007
- [Female] And one last question.

00:15:17.007 --> 00:15:20.020
So one of your number one tips

00:15:20.020 --> 00:15:22.348
is to learn how to communicate.

00:15:22.348 --> 00:15:26.245
So, could you give me one thing I could do

00:15:26.245 --> 00:15:27.870
that I could take away today

00:15:27.870 --> 00:15:30.679
that would make me a better communicator?

00:15:30.679 --> 00:15:32.961
- I would follow up with people

00:15:32.961 --> 00:15:34.873
after you communicate with them.

00:15:36.480 --> 00:15:38.480
It's about a feedback loop.

00:15:38.480 --> 00:15:39.870
- [Interviewer] Yeah.

00:15:39.870 --> 00:15:42.330
- And putting people in a
comfortable enough place

00:15:42.330 --> 00:15:44.110
to tell you the truth

00:15:44.110 --> 00:15:46.273
is an unbelievably important part of that.

00:15:47.290 --> 00:15:48.123
You know?

00:15:48.123 --> 00:15:50.100
- [Female] Yeah.
- But asking.

00:15:50.100 --> 00:15:51.400
It's a really powerful thing.

00:15:51.400 --> 00:15:53.170
I ask so many questions.

00:15:53.170 --> 00:15:55.610
Even in real time during speeches

00:15:55.610 --> 00:15:58.011
which is unusual behavior

00:15:58.011 --> 00:15:59.750
that I didn't know was unusual

00:15:59.750 --> 00:16:01.040
it's just my natural state

00:16:01.040 --> 00:16:02.469
to try to get feedback.

00:16:02.469 --> 00:16:05.041
So, asking people and being okay

00:16:05.041 --> 00:16:07.880
with feedback pro and con

00:16:07.880 --> 00:16:09.890
and trying to calibrate it in yourself.

00:16:09.890 --> 00:16:12.790
But, to me it's just a deep
respect for the audience.

00:16:12.790 --> 00:16:13.840
And again,

00:16:13.840 --> 00:16:16.090
I'm extroverted in high energy,

00:16:16.090 --> 00:16:19.410
so I'm always so worried that
people think that's important.

00:16:19.410 --> 00:16:20.530
There are so many people that are

00:16:20.530 --> 00:16:21.800
incredible communicators

00:16:21.800 --> 00:16:24.520
who are massively reserved.

00:16:24.520 --> 00:16:27.070
They just found their
authentic way to communicate.

00:16:28.029 --> 00:16:29.085
Right?

00:16:29.085 --> 00:16:31.752
(hip hop music)

00:16:37.570 --> 00:16:38.910
I don't think people understand

00:16:38.910 --> 00:16:40.590
what this level of content and impact

00:16:40.590 --> 00:16:42.200
looks like in 12 years.

00:16:42.200 --> 00:16:43.393
I'll be a young dude.

00:16:45.006 --> 00:16:47.650
I'm gonna be 55 years old!

00:16:47.650 --> 00:16:48.600
I'm gonna be a young dude!

00:16:48.600 --> 00:16:51.299
And I'm gonna be 55, like this!

00:16:51.299 --> 00:16:52.132
(laughs)

00:16:52.132 --> 00:16:52.965
You know, like,

00:16:53.844 --> 00:16:55.670
it's funny.

00:16:55.670 --> 00:16:56.503
- [D-Rock] Not gonna change.

00:16:56.503 --> 00:16:58.140
- You know, you look at

00:16:58.140 --> 00:16:59.170
how I see it is

00:16:59.170 --> 00:17:02.030
I look at rock 'n' roll and hippie guys.

00:17:02.030 --> 00:17:04.220
And not that I'm rock 'n' roll or hippie.

00:17:04.220 --> 00:17:06.620
But, at 55 they're like the same guy,

00:17:06.620 --> 00:17:08.210
I'm like, you're still a burner.

00:17:08.210 --> 00:17:09.043
Right?

00:17:09.043 --> 00:17:09.950
Or you still got,

00:17:09.950 --> 00:17:11.480
you're still rock 'n' roll.

00:17:11.480 --> 00:17:14.164
I'm still gonna be
entrepreneurship and hustler.

00:17:14.164 --> 00:17:16.831
(hip hop music)

00:17:19.270 --> 00:17:20.456
How many gyms?

00:17:20.456 --> 00:17:21.571
- [Man] One gym.

00:17:21.571 --> 00:17:23.082
3,000 square meters.

00:17:23.082 --> 00:17:24.108
So I have like

00:17:24.108 --> 00:17:25.550
which are easy to deal with.

00:17:25.550 --> 00:17:27.655
But then we have martial
arts instructors that

00:17:27.655 --> 00:17:28.860
have

00:17:28.860 --> 00:17:29.860
you can't jump over.

00:17:29.860 --> 00:17:31.210
To deal with,

00:17:31.210 --> 00:17:32.526
we treat 'em all like family,

00:17:32.526 --> 00:17:35.710
there's so many things that we do for 'em.

00:17:35.710 --> 00:17:37.065
But then they cross the line.

00:17:37.065 --> 00:17:38.575
- What line?

00:17:38.575 --> 00:17:42.286
- [Man] The drink fridge
and grab a drink and

00:17:42.286 --> 00:17:44.010
'I'll pay for that later',

00:17:44.010 --> 00:17:45.110
and it never gets paid for.

00:17:45.110 --> 00:17:47.043
We have a bar inside and cafe.

00:17:47.043 --> 00:17:49.060
- Well there's a couple things.

00:17:49.060 --> 00:17:50.410
I understand.

00:17:50.410 --> 00:17:51.560
A couple things that I think are

00:17:51.560 --> 00:17:53.690
super important to frame up.

00:17:53.690 --> 00:17:56.290
There's no such thing as

00:17:56.290 --> 00:17:58.840
employees taking advantage of an employer.

00:17:58.840 --> 00:18:00.500
There's things that

00:18:00.500 --> 00:18:02.450
'cause you're fundamentally in control.

00:18:03.543 --> 00:18:05.220
You can fire.

00:18:06.511 --> 00:18:08.160
What you're doing,

00:18:08.160 --> 00:18:09.610
like a lot of business owners are doing

00:18:09.610 --> 00:18:11.793
is you're amortising out the costs.

00:18:14.630 --> 00:18:15.770
You know,

00:18:15.770 --> 00:18:16.740
treating like family's

00:18:16.740 --> 00:18:19.450
also very dangerous framework.

00:18:19.450 --> 00:18:20.640
As you guys know I pump

00:18:20.640 --> 00:18:22.590
unlimited propaganda about culture,

00:18:22.590 --> 00:18:23.700
that's fine.

00:18:23.700 --> 00:18:26.020
But, you know,

00:18:26.020 --> 00:18:27.010
treating like family

00:18:27.010 --> 00:18:29.570
in the way that you're positioning it

00:18:29.570 --> 00:18:31.970
is something that I want to poke at,

00:18:31.970 --> 00:18:35.810
only because I think
that people can either

00:18:35.810 --> 00:18:40.030
get ideological, or
putting makeup on a truth.

00:18:40.030 --> 00:18:40.863
Right?

00:18:40.863 --> 00:18:43.060
So, a lot of people say,

00:18:43.060 --> 00:18:44.660
I treat my company like family,

00:18:44.660 --> 00:18:46.320
and I'll look at it carefully

00:18:46.320 --> 00:18:48.270
and I'm like, yeah of
course you do because

00:18:48.270 --> 00:18:50.460
you're using all these other triggers

00:18:50.460 --> 00:18:52.090
to subsidize the fact that you're

00:18:52.090 --> 00:18:53.460
underpaying market.

00:18:53.460 --> 00:18:55.010
Or you like,

00:18:55.010 --> 00:18:56.440
even if you're not underpaying market,

00:18:56.440 --> 00:18:58.030
you're doing it 'cause you want retention.

00:18:58.030 --> 00:19:03.030
So, you're doing everything
for the business.

00:19:03.270 --> 00:19:06.120
And, they don't own the business.

00:19:06.120 --> 00:19:08.570
And so, my dad, back to old school,

00:19:08.570 --> 00:19:10.143
used to get crazy.

00:19:10.143 --> 00:19:13.350
The biggest headbutts my dad and I had

00:19:13.350 --> 00:19:14.810
were about the employees.

00:19:14.810 --> 00:19:16.353
Period, by a thousand.

00:19:17.270 --> 00:19:19.660
The one fight that I never actually won

00:19:19.660 --> 00:19:21.040
with my dad,

00:19:21.040 --> 00:19:23.520
only out of, like, I
didn't want him to die,

00:19:23.520 --> 00:19:25.770
was I wanted to sell all our product

00:19:25.770 --> 00:19:29.140
in the store to our employees at cost.

00:19:29.140 --> 00:19:31.133
And it just drove him crazy.

00:19:32.520 --> 00:19:36.170
So, when somebody steals too many drinks,

00:19:36.170 --> 00:19:37.370
you fire them.

00:19:37.370 --> 00:19:39.260
I think the one mistake that you're making

00:19:39.260 --> 00:19:40.350
in my opinion,

00:19:40.350 --> 00:19:43.060
is you're being ideological about

00:19:43.060 --> 00:19:44.940
what you do for them.

00:19:44.940 --> 00:19:47.180
To me, when you want to do something,

00:19:47.180 --> 00:19:49.580
like not have them eat
the spinach anymore,

00:19:49.580 --> 00:19:51.120
you make that rule,

00:19:51.120 --> 00:19:53.000
and you deal with the
ramifications of people

00:19:53.000 --> 00:19:54.790
walking out or not.

00:19:54.790 --> 00:19:56.200
Life's about alternatives.

00:19:56.200 --> 00:19:57.920
If they can't get free spinach from you,

00:19:57.920 --> 00:19:59.260
they can go work at another gym

00:19:59.260 --> 00:20:00.093
and get free spinach,

00:20:00.093 --> 00:20:00.926
or maybe not.

00:20:01.801 --> 00:20:04.468
(hip hop music)

